{"cuisine/thai-american-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/thai-american-cuisine","n":"Thai-American cuisine","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Fusion cuisine","cuisine/fusion-cuisine"]],"sub":"Diaspora cuisine in United States of America","intro":[],"src":null,"wiki":"Thai-American cuisine","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"thai-american-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thai-American_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Fusion cuisine","cuisine/fusion-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Night + Market: Delicious Thai Food to Facilitate Drinking and Fun-Having Amongst Friends","ref":"cookbook/night-market-delicious-thai-food-to-facilitate-drinking-and-fun-having-amongst-friends","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Kris Yenbamroong with Garrett Snyder, 2017","note":"Thai cooking from the Los Angeles restaurant run by a Thai American chef.","url":"https://penguinrandomhouse.com/books/547465/night--market-by-kris-yenbamroong","suggested":true,"isbn":"9780451497871"}]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Fusion cuisine","cuisine/fusion-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas"},"cuisine/austrian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/austrian-cuisine","n":"Austrian cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Austria","intro":[["Austrian cuisine consists of many different local or regional cuisines. In addition to Viennese cuisine, which is predominantly based on the cooking traditions of the Habsburg Empire, there are independent regional traditions in all the states of Austria."],["The Austrian cuisine shares similarities with its neighboring countries in Central Europe, but particularly with the cuisines of Hungary (with which it was aligned as part of the Austro-Hungarian Empire), Bavaria, Bohemia and Northern Italy. Internationally, it is particularly well-known for its pastries, such as Kaiserschmarrn and apple strudel, and for meat-based dishes such as the Wiener schnitzel."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"austrian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austrian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Vienna Sunday Kitchen","ref":"site/vienna-sunday-kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"vienna-sunday.kitchen","note":"Viennese food blog of Austrian home cooking and pastries, with English-language recipes.","url":"https://www.vienna-sunday.kitchen/newest-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Lil Vienna","ref":"site/lilvienna-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lilvienna.com","note":"Austrian recipes from Ursula and David, two Austrians living in Boston.","url":"https://www.lilvienna.com/?p=1366","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Austrian Cooking and Baking","ref":"cookbook/austrian-cooking-and-baking","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Gretel Beer","note":"Long-standing English-language classic on Austrian dishes and baking, in print from Dover.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9780486232201","suggested":true,"isbn":"9780486232201"}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":15,"links":[["Blini","dish/blini"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Chicken paprikash","dish/chicken-paprikash"],["Dampfnudel","dish/dampfnudel"],["Egg puffs and soup pearls","dish/egg-puffs-and-soup-pearls"],["Gulyásleves","dish/gulyasleves"],["Leberkäse","dish/leberkase"],["Liptauer","dish/liptauer"],["Pancake","dish/pancake"],["Potato salad","dish/potato-salad"],["Sachertorte","dish/sachertorte"],["Spätzle","dish/spatzle"],["Strudel","dish/strudel"],["Tarhonya","dish/tarhonya"],["Zopf","dish/zopf"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Paprika","ingredient/paprika"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Jam","ingredient/jam"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"],["Wheat","ingredient/wheat"],["Cabbage","ingredient/cabbage"],["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Margarine","ingredient/margarine"],["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Bryndza","ingredient/bryndza"],["Cottage cheese","ingredient/cottage-cheese"],["Goat cheese","ingredient/goat-cheese"],["Quark","ingredient/quark"],["Quark cheese","ingredient/quark-cheese"],["Sheep milk","ingredient/sheep-milk"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Within Austrian cooking","count":1,"links":[["Viennese cuisine","cuisine/viennese-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/39/Grie%C3%9Fnockerlsuppe_cropped.jpg/500px-Grie%C3%9Fnockerlsuppe_cropped.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Christian Michelides","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grie%C3%9Fnockerlsuppe_cropped.jpg"}},"cuisine/moravian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/moravian-cuisine","n":"Moravian cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Czech cuisine","cuisine/czech-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Czechia","intro":[["Moravian cuisine encompasses the cooking styles, traditions and recipes associated with Moravia, a region of the Czech Republic (eastern part) and historically belongs to the Moravia, former historical country in Central Europe. Today, it is often perceived as an integral part of Czech cuisine, to which it has over the last century been artificially accommodated and mixed. Nevertheless, there is a large list of dishes, drinks and customs that are original only for Moravia."],["Moravian cuisine includes many pork and poultry meat and knödel dishes (koláčky, gulivary, pěry), and often uses flour, in the south many vegetables and fruits such as plums."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"moravian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moravian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Czech cuisine","cuisine/czech-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Czech cuisine","cuisine/czech-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/ae/Stuffed_paprica.jpg/500px-Stuffed_paprica.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Jan Sapák","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stuffed_paprica.jpg"}},"cuisine/coast-salish-foodways":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/coast-salish-foodways","n":"Coast Salish foodways","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Native American cuisine","cuisine/native-american-cuisine"]],"sub":"Indigenous foodways, Puget Sound and the Salish Sea, Washington","names":"Coast Salish peoples, including Muckleshoot and Nisqually","intro":[[["Salmon","ingredient/salmon"],", berries, elk and roots are the core of the Coast Salish diet around the Salish Sea. Muckleshoot guidelines call for a traditional meal like roasted salmon once a week, and intertribal ",["Camas","ingredient/camassia"]," harvests bring Elders and youth together."],["The Muckleshoot Food Sovereignty Project brings huckleberries, nettles, camas, salmon and elk back into everyday meals through classes, gardens and seminars, and cooks try new forms too, like elk burgers and huckleberry smoothies. At Nisqually, a community garden gives citizens free produce and syrups made from nettle, elderberry and fir tips."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"Northwest Indian Fisheries Commission, Muckleshoot food program fosters creative solutions","url":"https://nwifc.org/muckleshoot-food-program-fosters-creative-solutions/"},{"name":"Society of Ethnobiology, The Muckleshoot Food Sovereignty Project","url":"https://ethnobiology.org/muckleshoot-food-sovereignty-project-revitalizing-northwest-coastal-indian-food-culture"},{"name":"Cascade PBS, How tribes and local organizations are bolstering food sovereignty","url":"https://www.cascadepbs.org/news/2022/10/how-tribes-local-organizations-are-bolstering-food-sovereignty"},{"name":"Washington State Health Care Authority, Food and survival","url":"https://connections.hca.wa.gov/hca/2025/november/food-and-survival-why-fry-bread-is-not-a-novelty-food"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"coast-salish-foodways"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Native American cuisine","cuisine/native-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Native American cuisine","cuisine/native-american-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas"},"dish/ajvar":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/ajvar","n":"Ajvar","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Balkan cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Ajvar is a condiment made principally from sweet bell peppers and eggplants. The relish became a popular side dish throughout Yugoslavia after World War II and remains popular in Southeast Europe."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-ajvar"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ajvar"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Balkan cuisine","cuisine/balkan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"]]},{"h":"More from Balkan cuisine","links":[["Ayran","dish/ayran"],["Stuffed tomatoes","dish/stuffed-tomatoes"],["Tarator","dish/tarator"],["Torshi","dish/torshi"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/92/Ajvar_toast.jpg/500px-Ajvar_toast.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Popo le Chien","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ajvar_toast.jpg"}},"dish/buca-di-beppo":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/buca-di-beppo","n":"Buca di Beppo","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Buca di Beppo is an American restaurant chain specializing in Italian-American food. The chain of 40 establishments across the United States was previously a subsidiary of Planet Hollywood from 2008–2024. In November 2024, Main Street Capital Corporation invested over $30 million to acquire Buca di Beppo out of bankruptcy, hoping to position it for long-term success. To lead its attempted resurgence, Main Street partnered with Atlanta-based Jackmont Hospitality Inc. to oversee operations as the brand tries to embark on its next chapter."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-buca-di-beppo"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buca_di_Beppo"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","ref":"site/pastagrannies-substack-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","ref":"site/recipesfromitaly-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipesfromitaly.com","note":"Traditional Italian recipes written by Italian home cooks, organized by region and course.","url":"https://recipesfromitaly.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Manu's Menu","ref":"site/manusmenu-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"manusmenu.com","note":"Italian-born home cook Manuela sharing classic family and regional Italian dishes.","url":"https://www.manusmenu.com/about/about-this-site","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Italian cuisine","links":[["8½ Otto e Mezzo Bombana","dish/8-otto-e-mezzo-bombana"],["A16 (restaurant)","dish/a16-restaurant"],["Acquacotta","dish/acquacotta"],["Agliata","dish/agliata"],["Agnolotti","dish/agnolotti"],["Alfredo alla Scrofa","dish/alfredo-alla-scrofa"],["Alioto's","dish/alioto-s"],["Amalfi's Italian Restaurant","dish/amalfi-s-italian-restaurant"],["Amato's","dish/amato-s"],["Angelo's Civita Farnese","dish/angelo-s-civita-farnese"],["Antica Pizzeria Port'Alba","dish/antica-pizzeria-port-alba"],["Antico Pizza","dish/antico-pizza"],["Antipasto","dish/antipasto"],["Arancini","dish/arancini"],["ASK Italian","dish/ask-italian"],["Asti (restaurant)","dish/asti-restaurant"],["Ava Gene's","dish/ava-gene-s"],["Bamonte's","dish/bamonte-s"],["Bar del Corso","dish/bar-del-corso"],["Barbetta","dish/barbetta"],["Barbuto (restaurant)","dish/barbuto-restaurant"],["Bella Italia","dish/bella-italia"],["Beppi's Restaurant","dish/beppi-s-restaurant"],["Bertucci's","dish/bertucci-s"],["BiCE Ristorante","dish/bice-ristorante"],["Biscotti","dish/biscotti"],["Black' Smith","dish/black-smith"],["Bocca di Lupo","dish/bocca-di-lupo"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Bombolone","dish/bombolone"],["Budino","dish/budino"],["Buona","dish/buona"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Caffé Vittoria","dish/caffe-vittoria"],["Camille's (Providence, Rhode Island)","dish/camille-s-providence-rhode-island"],["Campisi's Egyptian Restaurant","dish/campisi-s-egyptian-restaurant"],["Cannelloni","dish/cannelloni"],["Capellini","dish/capellini"],["Caravaggio (restaurant)","dish/caravaggio-restaurant"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/b3/Buca_di_Beppo_Restaurant_Livonia_Michigan.jpg/500px-Buca_di_Beppo_Restaurant_Livonia_Michigan.jpg","w":500,"h":267,"by":"Dwight Burdette","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buca_di_Beppo_Restaurant_Livonia_Michigan.jpg"}},"dish/country-dough":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/country-dough","n":"Country Dough","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"