"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Duck is the common name for numerous species of waterfowl in the family Anatidae. Ducks are generally smaller and shorter-necked than swans and geese, which are members of the same family. Divided among several subfamilies, they are a form taxon; they do not represent a monophyletic group (the group of all descendants of a single common ancestral species), since swans and geese are not considered ducks. Ducks are mostly aquatic birds and may be found in both fresh water and sea water."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-duck"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duck"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Lontong dekem","dish/lontong-dekem"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Meat of ducks, fresh or chilled","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":6659915,"top":[["China","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",5333860],["Vietnam","cuisine/vietnamese-cuisine",171807],["France","cuisine/french-cuisine",162230],["Thailand","cuisine/thai-cuisine",82051],["Taiwan","cuisine/taiwan-cuisine",79544],["South Korea","cuisine/korean-cuisine",71857],["Hungary","cuisine/hungarian-cuisine",69600],["Malaysia","cuisine/malaysian-cuisine",69359],["Poland","cuisine/polish-cuisine",66068],["Bangladesh","cuisine/bangladeshi-cuisine",62271],["Myanmar","cuisine/burmese-cuisine",59978],["United States of America","cuisine/american-cuisine",58484],["Egypt","cuisine/egyptian-cuisine",45006],["India","cuisine/indian-cuisine",44020],["Indonesia","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",42284]]}},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Krupuk","ingredient/krupuk"],["Lontong","ingredient/lontong"],["Serundeng","ingredient/serundeng"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisi