 Created by Iraqi Jewish merchants in Bombay who purportedly shipped mangoes in vinegar back to Baghdad, Amba bears a resemblance to chutneys from South Asia. The spicy, sweet and sour sauce is typically made of pickled green mangoes, vinegar, salt, turmeric, chilies, and fenugreek. It is enjoyed in various Middle Eastern countries, particularly in Israel, as well as to a lesser extent in Europe and the United States (largely among the Iraqi, Jewish, and Assyrian diaspora)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-amba-condiment"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amba_(condiment)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Israeli cuisine","cuisine/israeli-cuisine",[["Sabich","dish/sabich"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Amba","ingredient/amba"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Eggplant","ingredient/eggplant"],["Hummus","ingredient/hummus"],["Israeli salad","ingredient/israeli-salad"],["Laffa","ingredient/laffa"],["Parsley","ingredient/parsley"],["Pita","ingredient/pita"],["Salad","ingredient/salad"],["Tahini","ingredient/tahini"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/9/99/Amba.jpg","w":500,"h":388,"by":"Tatan48","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amba.jpg"}},"dish/tipatipa":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/tipatipa","n":"Tipatipa","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Tipatipa is a typical of Batak snack from Porsea, Toba Samosir, North Sumatra."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-tipatipa"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tipatipa"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Rice","ingredient/rice"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","ref":"site/dailycookingquest-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","not